From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?=EC=8B=AC=EC=83=81=EC=9B=90?= <dev.chamomile@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 12:34:22 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] block: async engine on platform::async_io

Why: the Async block engine is io_uring, which only Linux has.

What: the block device's async engine submits through `platform::async_io`
(io_uring on Linux, worker threads with F_FULLFSYNC or FlushFileBuffers
elsewhere, same submission/completion model and queue limits). The
io_uring kernel tests run only on Linux; the block device reads file
identity and type through each host's metadata.

Test: block device and io tests on each host; a guest reads and writes a
drive with `io_engine: Async`.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
